{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdZHVHkVHsriYmoVUbF8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Apple's Speech framework has no module for working out who is speaking, so anyone transcribing a conversation with SpeechAnalyzer gets text without speaker labels. AnySpeechRecognizer adds one called SpeakerDiarizer, which runs NVIDIA's Streaming Sortformer on Core ML. It is installed and run alongside an Apple or Parakeet transcriber in the same SpeechAnalyzer, on the same timeline. The package's SpeakerTimeline collects the diarizer's results and attributes each timed word to a speaker, which is what allows a transcript to be printed by speaker turn.\n\nThe diarizer tracks up to four speakers, including when they talk over each other. That ceiling is relevant for meetings with larger groups. The default model is Sortformer v2, and v2.1 is available as an option. NVIDIA trained v2.1 with more meeting data, and the authors report that it was more accurate on meetings in their own measurements. The announcement does not give diarization error figures, so how much more accurate is not something the article establishes.\n\nSpeaker labels do not fix transcription accuracy in overlapping speech. On AMI meeting recordings, where people talk over each other, every engine the authors tested had a word error rate above 23%, compared with 1.43% to 4.73% on the LibriSpeech file and live runs they report for the Parakeet models. The authors describe meetings as hard for everyone, and their measurements were on a single M4 Max Mac Studio running macOS 27.0.1, with no iPhone testing yet.\n\nThe engine choice also affects what a transcript contains. Qwen3-ASR gives one final result per segment of up to 40 seconds, with no word timing, so word-level speaker attribution is a reason to start with Parakeet or Apple's transcriber. That follows from the article's description of the diarizer's pairings and Qwen's missing word timing, and the article does not state it as a rule."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1403,"cache_read_input_tokens":10421,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1403},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cd18c5f8-2302-4498-9962-d47d36bcbea1","uuid":"8f82fb10-067f-482b-a6b4-3384db07e9aa","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:34:46.693Z","request_id":"req_011CgdZHV4MsaT74GoefUxDh"}
